	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/476/G047609/20261009048/">
<ns1:title>"Proseca" Adds "at" to Its Rhythm Game Track List as Part of Its 6th Anniversary Song Addition Campaign</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/476/G047609/20261009048/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-11T15:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>

</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104930/20261011002/">
<ns1:title>"Huni Kuin: Beya Xin' Bena" is a 2D action game [BGS2026] featuring artwork and voice acting by Amazonian villagers.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104930/20261011002/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-11T12:07:36+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　"HuniKuin: BeyaXin'Bena," a game developed with the involvement of Amazonian indigenous peoples, was on display at "BrasilGameShow 2026." The game is based on myths passed down through the tribe and is scheduled for release in the first quarter of 2027. We spoke with Guilherme Meneses, an anthropologist who has been working with the Huni Kuin people for over 14 years.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104929/20261010013/">
<ns1:title>Survive hell in a game of rigged poker. “Hell Hold’em,” where “666” is the strongest hand, is a highly anticipated title that masterfully blends roguelike elements with Texas Hold’em.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104929/20261010013/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T18:13:29+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　At the “SAGABarcelonaGameFest2026” gaming event, numerous indie titles that have garnered attention for their original ideas are on display. Among them, “HellHold’em”—a deck-building roguelike set in Hell—is capturing the attention of attendees with its unique world and robust gameplay.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/038/G003821/20261009008/">
<ns1:title>Weekly Steam Plaza, Issue 174: “Clive Barker’s Hellraiser: Revival” and “Star Wars: Galactic Racer” Now Available</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/038/G003821/20261009008/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T18:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　"Weekly Steam Plaza" brings you the latest notable titles and sale information from Steam released this week. This week saw the release of “Clive Barker’s Hellraiser: Revival,” based on the horror film series “Hellraiser,” and the roguelike racing game “Star Wars: Galactic Racer.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261010010/">
<ns1:title>An exclusive look inside Scopely, the company that has transformed Barcelona into a major development hub in Southern Europe. Introducing a mobile game company that’s actually quite familiar to Japanese audiences.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261010010/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T17:39:28+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Barcelona is buzzing with excitement as it hosts “SAGABarcelonaGameFest2026.” Scopely is one of the companies supporting this city as it evolves into a hub for game development. Let’s take a look at this company, which operates “ScopelyExplore”—a service you may have seen in “Pokémon GO.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/779/G077989/20261010005/">
<ns1:title>Chief, it’s time to board! Let’s look back on the journey of “18TRIP” and head to “HAMA TRANSIT CHECK-IN to Season 2,” where 30 district chiefs await [PR]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/779/G077989/20261010005/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T16:38:48+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Chief, the flight to Season 2 is about to depart! The “HAMATRANSITCHECK-INtoSeason2” promotional campaign for “18TRIP” is currently on display at Minatomirai Station through October 12. From an exhibition looking back on Season 1 to full-body panels of 30 ward mayors, here’s our report on the venue transformed into an “airport.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/004/G100471/20261010011/">
<ns1:title>Passing on the story of a tragedy that occurred in their hometown through a game. “ARIDA 2: Rise of the Brave,” developed by a studio in Bahia [BGS2026]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/004/G100471/20261010011/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T16:20:53+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　At the “BrasilGameShow2026,” which opened on October 9, 2026, AocaGameLab’s “ARIDA2: Rise of the Brave” was on display. This was their second appearance following “gamescomlatam2026” in May, and the demo version available this time could be played in Japanese. Filipe Pereira, CEO and producer, spoke about why he chose to turn the history of his hometown into a game.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/476/G047609/20261009047/">
<ns1:title>"Proseca" Adds "Hydrangea" to Its Rhythm Game Track List; 3D Music Video Also Released</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/476/G047609/20261009047/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T15:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>

</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/036/G103670/20261010009/">
<ns1:title>Prologue video for “Shikai” released. A brand-new occult suspense film from the staff behind the “Science Adventure” series.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/036/G103670/20261010009/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T14:54:14+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　MAGES. has released a prologue video for its new adventure game, *Shikai*, scheduled for release in the winter of 2026. This unique title comes from the team behind the “Science Adventure” series—which has explored the world’s mysteries through “logic and science” in titles such as “STEINS;GATE”—and delves into “supernatural phenomena” that cannot be explained by science.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261010007/">
<ns1:title>"SAGA Barcelona Game Fest 2026," one of Southern Europe's largest gaming events, which combines three separate events, will be held. A legend of video game music from Japan, the guest country, will also be in attendance.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261010007/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T14:51:11+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　"SAGABarcelonaGameFest2026" is currently being held in Barcelona, Spain, from October 9 to 11. This new gaming event combines three separate events, and Japan has been selected as the guest country for its inaugural edition. A talk session featuring Miki Higashino and Manami Matsumae will also be held.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261010008/">
<ns1:title>From the Switch 2 demo stations to the replica sword shop: A photo report from the BGS venue, where merchandise booths take center stage [BGS2026]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261010008/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T13:10:54+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　At the "BrasilGameShow 2026" gaming event, taking place from October 9 to 12, 2026, alongside hands-on demo booths run by game developers, shops selling figurines, replica swords, and used retro games are packed together, and there’s also a large section dedicated to arcade machines and motion simulators. Here are some photos from the venue on the first day.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261010006/">
<ns1:title>"Brasil Game Show 2026" Kicks Off. Sega Unveils New "Brazil" Map for "Crazy Taxi: World Tour" at Opening Event [BGS2026]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261010006/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T12:02:19+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 9, 2026, “BrasilGameShow 2026” kicked off in São Paulo, Brazil. Before the doors opened on the first day, the “BGS Conference” was held, where exhibitors introduced their new titles and products. Sega revealed, through a world-premiere video, that “Brazil” will appear in the story mode of “Crazy Taxi: World Tour.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/985/G098513/20261009024/">
<ns1:title>Just three dice can unleash tens of millions of power. “DiceVaders” is a “dice roguelike” that takes board-game-style engine-building to the digital extreme [Play Report]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/985/G098513/20261009024/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T12:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　"DiceVaders," developed by Pengonauts, is a roguelike dice game set in the same universe as "StarVaders." Players roll three dice and chain their effects together to achieve a high score. Let’s take a look at what makes this game so appealing—it lets you experience the fun of board-game-style engine-building in a digital format.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104928/20261009060/">
<ns1:title>A "QUEEN'S GUARD" Play Report That Reflects the Passion of Experienced Swordsmen. An Action-Adventure Game Where You Protect the Princess as Her Bodyguard [OIGS2026]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104928/20261009060/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T10:30:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　At the “OSAKA INDIE GAME SUMMIT 2026,” held on October 3 and 4, a demo version of MIBUKI STUDIO’s action adventure game “QUEEN’S GUARD” was on display. Let’s take a look at the realistic feel of the combat—which reflects the developer’s expertise in swordsmanship—and the game itself, scheduled for release in 2027, along with comments from the developer.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/810/G081093/20261007048/">
<ns1:title>Tickets for “Lilia Game Music Selection Vol. 3: Kenji Ito with Tsutomu Narita” went on sale today. The event will be held in Kawaguchi on March 13, 2027.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/810/G081093/20261007048/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T10:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　General ticket sales for the concert “Lilia Game Music Selection Vol. 3: Kenji Ito with Tsutomu Narita,” to be held on March 13, 2027, at the Kawaguchi General Cultural Center Lilia, began today (October 10) at 10:00 a.m. Tickets are 8,000 yen (tax included) for all reserved seats.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104870/20261008026/">
<ns1:title>Use your mouse to dash like a flash of lightning and slice enemies in half! A play report on the ultra-high-speed action game “▽△Slash,” created by a student team from HAL Osaka [OIGS2026]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104870/20261008026/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T09:30:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　At the “OSAKA INDIE GAME SUMMIT 2026,” held on October 3 and 4, a demo version of “▽△Slash (Tri-Slash),” a PC action game developed by students at HAL Osaka Vocational School, was on display. In this title, players can experience an exhilarating sense of speed as a half-human, half-yōkai girl cuts down yokai with overwhelming force.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104923/20261009056/">
<ns1:title>The terror of navigating the darkness by candlelight and the psychological unease that creeps up on you. A hands-on report on “Kindling Hour,” a click-based psychological horror adventure game [OIGS2026]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104923/20261009056/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T09:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　At the “OSAKA INDIE GAME SUMMIT 2026,” held on October 3 and 4, a demo version of “Kindling Hour,” a psychological horror adventure by game sound designer KuwaPon, was showcased. Here, we’ll share the unique feel of this unconventional title—where you encounter strange phenomena as you venture through the darkness—along with comments from the developer.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/631/G063178/20261010004/">
<ns1:title>"Dollfro 2" 2nd Anniversary Orchestral Concert "The Dolls' White Nocturne" Confirmed; Some Newly Drawn Illustrations Revealed</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/631/G063178/20261010004/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T07:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 9, 2026, Samborn Japan will hold an orchestral concert titled “The Dolls’ White Nocturne” to commemorate the second anniversary of the launch of the smartphone and PC RPG "Dolls Frontline 2: Exilium," to be held on January 15, 2027, at the Rene Kodaira Grand Hall in Tokyo.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/882/G088208/20261006034/">
<ns1:title>"Sonic Racing Cross World," which has celebrated its first anniversary, is moving on to Season 2. Get an early look at "Godzilla" and "Evangelion" collaboration tracks and new game modes.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/882/G088208/20261006034/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T05:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Sega plans to release the latest DLC, “Season Pass 2,” for its currently available racing game “Sonic Racing Cross World” on November 4. We got an early look at the first installment, the “Godzilla Pack,” and the second installment, the “Evangelion Pack.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/649/G064915/20261010003/">
<ns1:title>"Rage of the Wolves: City of the Wolves" Welcomes "Reina" from Tekken 8! Scheduled for release in December to wrap up Season 3</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/649/G064915/20261010003/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T02:06:27+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　SNK announced today (October 10, 2026) at “EVO France 2026,” currently being held in Nice, France, that “Reina” from “Tekken 8” will be joining the roster as a new DLC character for “Fatal Fury: City of the Wolves.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/402/G040245/20261010002/">
<ns1:title>The "Knives Out" × "Don Quijote" collaboration kicks off today. Take a commemorative photo with the giant Npen for a chance to win in-game items.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/402/G040245/20261010002/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T00:57:13+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　NetEase Games announced today (October 10, 2026) that it has launched a collaboration between the battle royale game "Knives Out" and the discount retailer "Don Quijote." During the collaboration period, “Donpen,” Don Quijote’s official mascot, will appear in giant form on the “Storm Peninsula” map.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/639/G063965/20261010001/">
<ns1:title>"Board Game Arena" Officially Launches "Puppet Master: Duel," a Two-Player Remake of the Classic Board Game</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/639/G063965/20261010001/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-10T00:30:02+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 7, 2026, Asmodee Digital officially launched Z-Man Games’ board game “Citadels Duel” on “Board Game Arena,” the online board game site it operates. This game is a two-player reimagining of “Puppet Master,” in which players use the abilities of their roles to compete for control of buildings in a shared 4×4 grid city.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104924/20261009059/">
<ns1:title>Build a new pantheon in a post-Ragnarok world! “Aftergods,” a top-down action RPG featuring the children of the gods in battle, has been announced.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104924/20261009059/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T23:29:50+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Norsfell announced its new title, “Aftergods,” today (October 9, 2026). In this top-down survival action RPG, you play as the child of a god who survived Ragnarok, gathering followers to build a new pantheon. You’ll use divine powers to survive, such as gathering resources through storms and summoning temples.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/630/G063081/20261009057/">
<ns1:title>"Zenless Zone Zero" Ver. 3.3 is set to launch on October 21. The Steam version is also scheduled for release at the same time. Details about a collaboration with "Honkai: Star Rail" have also been revealed.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/630/G063081/20261009057/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T22:19:14+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　HoYoverse released a preview video today (October 9, 2026) for the action RPG “Zenless Zone Zero” and announced that Version 3.3, “Take Flight Once More,” will be released on October 21. This update will introduce S-Rank Agents “Fionie” and “Severian,” along with new mecha combat content.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/993/G099381/20261009054/">
<ns1:title>"Forever Ago," a narrative adventure game in which an elderly man travels to places from his past in a minivan, is now available.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/993/G099381/20261009054/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T21:45:45+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 8, 2026, Annapurna Interactive released “ForeverAgo,” a new title developed by ThirdShift. This road trip adventure game follows “Alfred,” an elderly man who has reached a tragic turning point in his life, as he embarks on a journey to revisit the places where he shared memories with his lover, “Audrey.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104922/20261009055/">
<ns1:title>Turn a walkable city into one where cars are a must! “Car Park Capital,” a “satirical” management sim that makes residents car-dependent, launches in Early Access</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104922/20261009055/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T21:37:50+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　MicroProse Software today (October 9, 2026) launched Early Access on Steam for “CarPark Capital,” a new PC game developed by Hilkojj Interactive. It is a management sim in which players convert residential properties into parking lots and use advertising to encourage residents to become car-dependent in order to turn a profit.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/986/G098698/20261009053/">
<ns1:title>You are a beta tester for a system that lets you freely correspond with the dead. "Posthumors," an adventure game where you communicate with ghosts, has launched in Early Access on Steam.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/986/G098698/20261009053/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T21:07:10+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Anisa Cafe launched early access for the PC game “Posthumors” today. This adventure game involves corresponding with ghosts to communicate with the afterlife. As a test user selected for a system that allows you to freely correspond with the dead, you’ll exchange letters with ghosts detained in a hellish holding facility.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/666/G066636/20261009052/">
<ns1:title>"Nobunaga's Ambition: Hado" Begins Accepting Applications for Its 4th Anniversary Official Fan Gathering. Executive Producer Tomohiro Kuroda and cast members from the official livestream are scheduled to attend.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/666/G066636/20261009052/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T20:50:58+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Koei Tecmo Games announced today (October 9, 2026) that it has begun accepting applications for the official 4th-anniversary meetup for *Nobunaga’s Ambition: Hado*. The event is scheduled to take place on December 6 at the KT Building in Yokohama. The event will feature opportunities to interact with the executive producer and cast members of the official livestream, as well as a quiz contest. The event is limited to 40 participants, and the application deadline is October 18 at 11:59 PM.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/037/G103786/20261009051/">
<ns1:title>"Clive Barker's Hellraiser: Revival," a survival horror series that continues the official storyline of the "Hellraiser" film franchise, is now streaming.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/037/G103786/20261009051/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T20:45:20+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 8, 2026, SaberInteractive released its new title, “Clive Barker’s Hellraiser: Revival.” This first-person survival horror game follows the canonical storyline of the series, which began with the 1987 horror film “Hellraiser.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/760/G076029/20261009049/">
<ns1:title>A Party with 63 Hololive Members in Dresses! A Peek Inside the Tokyo Venue for “hololive Grand Reception ~An Invitation Filled with Gratitude~”</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/760/G076029/20261009049/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T20:33:37+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　The “hololive” 9th Anniversary Event, “hololive Grand Reception ~An Invitation Filled with Gratitude~,” will be held sequentially at a total of four venues—starting in Tokyo on October 10, 2026, and continuing in Osaka, Nagoya, and Fukuoka. A preview event for members of the press was held the day before the opening, so I’d like to report on the event, focusing primarily on photos.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

