	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/651/G065198/20261009033/">
<ns1:title>"Fūen-den: Where Winds Meet" will introduce the new region "Qingzhou" on October 15. Information on the weapon "Mai-Aya Drum" and three new wild bosses has also been revealed.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/651/G065198/20261009033/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T18:52:59+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　NetEase Games and Everstone Studio announced today (October 9, 2026) that they will add the new region “Qingzhou” to the wuxia open-world action RPG *Feng Yan Zhuan: Where Winds Meet* on October 15. Additionally, the “Wuying Drum”—a weapon that fuses dance and martial arts—and three new wild bosses will also be added.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/918/G091863/20261009030/">
<ns1:title>A report on “SONIC the Exhibition -ACROSS GENERATIONS-,” an exhibition commemorating the 35th anniversary of “Sonic.” The exhibition features artworks brimming with love and rare, never-before-seen materials.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/918/G091863/20261009030/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T18:39:05+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　"SONIC the Exhibition—ACROSS GENERATIONS—," an event commemorating the 35th anniversary of Sega's iconic character "Sonic," is being held from October 9 to November 1, 2026, at PARCO FACTORY on the 7th floor of the Ikebukuro PARCO Main Building. This article provides a look at the media preview held on October 8.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/760/G076023/20261009032/">
<ns1:title>Explore the city while being watched by giant police officers and aim to escape using a variety of methods. A demo version of the stealth adventure game "Militsioner," featuring the entire first act, is now available to the public.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/760/G076023/20261009032/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T18:27:16+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　CRITICALREFLEX today began distributing a demo version of the new game "Militsioner," developed by TALLBOYS, on Steam. The demo includes Act 1 in its entirety, and features significant improvements to the city, its residents, the giants, and the exploration paths since the playtest conducted in August 2025.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/982/G098251/20261009028/">
<ns1:title>"Satori Chuunibyou Counseling Room - Translator of the Second Reality" Released on Steam as an Early Access Title. Try to decipher the true feelings of visitors suffering from chuunibyou.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/982/G098251/20261009028/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T18:17:21+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Fine released the early access version of the PC game “Satori Chuunibyou Counseling Room: Translator of the Second Reality” on Steam today. This title is a psychological mystery adventure game centered on the theme of “chuunibyou.” As the director of the counseling center, the player must decipher the “Second Reality”—an otherworldly worldview believed in by visitors suffering from “chuunibyou.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/968/G096803/20261009031/">
<ns1:title>"Order of the Sinking Star," the new game from Jonathan Blow, creator of "The Witness" and "Braid," is out today.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/968/G096803/20261009031/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T18:07:57+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　ArcGames released its new title, “Order of the Sinking Star,” today (October 9, 2026). Created by Jonathan Blow, known for “The Witness” and “Braid,” this puzzle-adventure game challenges players’ intellect with over 1,000 puzzles.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/238/G023885/20261009029/">
<ns1:title>Collaboration illustrations between "Granblue Fantasy" and Sanrio characters have been unveiled for the first time. Eight characters, including Sandalphon and Narmea, make an appearance.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/238/G023885/20261009029/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T18:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 9, 2026, Cygames unveiled the first illustration as part of a follow-up announcement regarding its collaboration with Sanrio Characters, which will take place at “Granblue Festival 2026.” The illustration features characters from “Granblue Fantasy”—such as Filkiss, Sandalphon, and Narmea—alongside Sanrio characters.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/035/G103503/20261009027/">
<ns1:title>"Japanese Ramen Simulator" Early Access Version Finally Released. Work together with up to 6 players to run your own specialty ramen shop.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/035/G103503/20261009027/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T17:05:55+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Wild Dog released the early access version of its PC game “Japanese Ramen Simulator” on Steam today. This game is a ramen shop management simulation that supports up to six players. The original release date was September 28, but the developer used the extra time gained from the delay to add dan dan noodles and a new ingredient, “garlic chives.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/189/G018964/20261009022/">
<ns1:title>Paramount Pictures is planning a feature-length live-action film set in the world of "Cyberpunk 2077." CD PROJEKT RED, the game's developer, will also participate in the production.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/189/G018964/20261009022/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T16:44:28+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　It has been revealed that Paramount Pictures is planning a feature-length live-action film set in the world of “Cyberpunk 2077.” Lorenz di Bonaventura, who worked on the “Transformers” series, will serve as producer, and CD Projekt RED will also participate in the production.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104912/20261009025/">
<ns1:title>"Reply Signals - Echoes Still Wait," a dialogue-based adventure game where you talk to captive children and help them escape, has released a demo on Steam.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/049/G104912/20261009025/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T16:43:43+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Tesaria Studio released a demo version of its PC game “Reply Signals—Echoes Still Wait” on Steam today. This interactive adventure game puts players in the role of a child trapped in a closed-off world and the “someone” who is the only person connected to them, helping the child escape through chat.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/343/G034351/20261009026/">
<ns1:title>"Infection × Girl" will end service at 2:00 p.m. on December 10, 2026. This brings to a close a history spanning approximately 10 years since the smartphone version launched in August 2016.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/343/G034351/20261009026/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T16:27:50+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 8, 2026, Age announced that it would terminate service for the smartphone RPG “Infection × Girl” at 2:00 PM on December 10, 2026. The game, which launched for iOS and Android in August 2016, will bring its nearly 10-year run to a close.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/625/G062571/20261009023/">
<ns1:title>"Rainbow Six Mobile" will end service on January 15, 2027. The next season will be released next week as scheduled.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/625/G062571/20261009023/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T15:58:18+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Ubisoft announced today that it will discontinue service for “Rainbow Six Mobile” on January 15, 2027. Following a soft launch in 2023, the game was released worldwide on February 23, 2026, meaning service will end after approximately 11 months. The next season will be released next week as scheduled.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/937/G093723/20261009020/">
<ns1:title>All you can see is the back of the girl. "Cyan Heart," a horror adventure game played from a first-person perspective, is now available on Steam.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/937/G093723/20261009020/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T15:39:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Independent developer Shoei Sio released his new title, “CyanHeart,” today (October 9, 2026). The game is a horror exploration puzzle adventure played from the perspective of a girl who continuously films herself with a camera.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/998/G099824/20261009021/">
<ns1:title>"Professor Layton and the New World of Steam": The early purchase bonus for the physical edition and the pre-order bonus for the digital edition is "Series Sound Selection."</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/998/G099824/20261009021/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T15:36:33+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Level-5 announced today (October 9, 2026) the early purchase bonus for the physical edition and the pre-order bonus for the digital edition of *Professor Layton and the New World of Steam*, which is scheduled for release on December 10. The bonus for this title is the “Series Sound Selection,” which features all 11 tracks from the Layton series.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/999/G999905/20261009019/">
<ns1:title>Xbox Establishes New Division "XP" to Oversee Non-Gaming IP Development; Kayleen Walters, Who Helped Grow the "Minecraft" Merchandise Business, Appointed President</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/999/G999905/20261009019/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T15:27:17+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 8, 2026, Microsoft announced the establishment of a new Xbox division called “XP.” This division will consolidate functions—including film and television, merchandising, brand partnerships, and events—that were previously spread across multiple teams. Kayleen Walters, who has led Mojang, will serve as president of the division.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/011/G101152/20261009018/">
<ns1:title>Songs from *The Legend of Zelda: Majora's Mask* are now available on *Nintendo Music*. The collection includes a total of 111 tracks, such as the background music for "Clock Town."</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/011/G101152/20261009018/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T15:07:24+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Nintendo announced today (October 9, 2026) that it has added music from *The Legend of Zelda: Majora's Mask* to "Nintendo Music," a music service for Nintendo Switch Online subscribers.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/015/G101558/20261009015/">
<ns1:title>"Dragon's Dogma 2: Dark Arisen" is out today. The game features a story set in the far-northern land of "Norgan," as well as 12 new dungeons containing rare equipment.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/015/G101558/20261009015/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T14:47:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Capcom released "Dragon's Dogma 2: Dark Arisen" today. This title expands upon the open-world action game "Dragon's Dogma 2," which was released in March 2024, by adding new storylines and experiences. It features story content set in the far-northern land of “Norgan,” as well as 12 dungeons containing rare equipment.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/276/G027611/20261009014/">
<ns1:title>The new "Cities: Skylines" DLCs, "Mansions &amp; Manors" and "Holiday Getaways," will be released on October 28, 2026. "Blueprint Beats Radio," an in-game radio station featuring 16 tracks, will also launch on the same day.</ns1:title>
