	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261009001/">
<ns1:title>"Kazuki Takahashi Original Art Exhibition": The "Final Turn" of the Battle City Arc Finals is brought to life with newly recorded voice acting. Advance ticket sales for the first half of the exhibition will begin on October 10 at 10:00 a.m.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999110/20261009001/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T10:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Shueisha announced today (October 9, 2026) that announced that advance ticket sales on a first-come, first-served basis for the first half of the “Kazuki Takahashi Original Art Exhibition: YU-GI-OH! ARTWORKS,” which opens on December 12, will begin at 10:00 a.m. on October 10, and revealed details about the “Special Video—As Friends!!—” to be screened at the venue. In conjunction with this announcement, information regarding the official exhibition catalog, a themed café, and additional original merchandise was also revealed.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/709/G070944/20261006038/">
<ns1:title>"Phantom Blade Zero" Features a "Pyramid Structure" That Combines High-Speed Action with an RPG Foundation [Interview]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/709/G070944/20261006038/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T09:00:30+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　S-GAME held a hands-on demo event in Beijing, China, for “PhantomBladeZero,” a PS5/PC game set for release on October 29. Following the six-hour hands-on session, founder and game director Liang Qiwei (aka Soulframe) and sound producer Bo Caisheng participated in a joint interview with Japanese media. We’ll cover everything from the number of bosses and difficulty levels to AI and the game’s action mechanics.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/709/G070944/20261006026/">
<ns1:title>"Phantom Blade Zero" is a wuxia action RPG that features not only intense swordplay but also in-depth exploration. Even with just rapid button presses, you can become the star of a kung fu movie.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/709/G070944/20261006026/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T09:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　S-GAME held a hands-on demo event in Beijing, China, for “PhantomBladeZero,” a PS5/PC game set for release on October 29. Attendees were able to play through Chapter 1 in its entirety—a session lasting about five hours—as well as two boss battles taken from the latter half of the game. Beyond the high-speed swordplay, the demo left a lasting impression with its strong emphasis on exploration and the dramatic presentation that made even simple movements feel like a theatrical gesture.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/587/G058755/20261008048/">
<ns1:title>The anime "Ghost of Tsushima: The Tale of the Shadow Man" is scheduled for release in 2028. Additional staff and cast information was also revealed at the same time.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/587/G058755/20261008048/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T08:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　It was announced at "New York Comic Con," which opened on October 8, 2026 (local time), that the anime "Ghost of Tsushima: Tales of the Dark" is scheduled for release sometime in 2028. Further details regarding the music, sound director, and cast were also revealed.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/025/G102544/20261008005/">
<ns1:title>"Dressmaker" (Akane's Steam Pick Up!), where you create dresses for the townspeople from patterns</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/025/G102544/20261008005/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T08:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　In today’s “Akane’s SteamPickUp!”, we’re introducing “Dressmaker,” a dressmaking simulator where you handle every step of the dress-making process yourself—from placing the patterns to ensuring precise seams. Based on the rough requests from townspeople who visit your shop, you’ll decide on a design, buy fabric, place the pattern while checking the grain, cut the fabric, and sew it together on a sewing machine.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999104/20261006020/">
<ns1:title>An era where imagination becomes content is just around the corner. Ken Kutaragi, the creator of PlayStation, discusses entertainment in the age of AI [Interview]</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999104/20261006020/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T07:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　We spoke with Ken Kutaragi, known as the father of the PlayStation, about the history of technological innovation in the gaming industry and the future of entertainment brought about by AI. Kutaragi, who says, “Imagination becomes content,” shares his vision for the future of games and AI. We took a closer look at his outlook.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104888/20261008052/">
<ns1:title>The calendar remains frozen on the eve of the millennium—how did this Chinese town meet its end? The new psychological horror game “Soul Scream” is set for release in 2027.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104888/20261008052/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-09T02:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　IOIGAMER announced today (October 9, 2026) that it will release “Kyo Kon,” a first-person psychological horror game featuring a cinematic narrative experience, sometime in 2027. Players will investigate the reasons behind the downfall of a small Chinese town where time seems to have stood still just before the dawn of a new century.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/649/G064915/20261008051/">
<ns1:title>"Fatal Fury: CotW" × "Tokyo Revengers": Trailer Introducing Collaboration Characters Released. Mikey &amp; Draken Head to South Town</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/649/G064915/20261008051/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T22:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　SNK announced today (October 8, 2026) that it has released a character trailer for “Manjiro Sano (Mikey),” a collaboration character from the anime “Tokyo Revengers” joining the fighting game “Fatal Fury: City of the Wolves” and “Ken Ryūgūji (Draken)” from the anime “Tokyo Revengers.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104885/20261008047/">
<ns1:title>"Let's Organize the Capybaras!," a tidying-up game where you place 4,800 adorable capybara toys on the correct shelves, is now available on Steam.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104885/20261008047/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T21:04:53+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　CapybaraKoala began distributing its PC game "Let's Tidy Up the Capybaras!" on Steam today. This game is a tidying-up game in which players must correctly organize as many as 4,800 cute capybara toys across 12 themed areas.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/900/G090034/20261008050/">
<ns1:title>Survive alongside your friends in a barren, ice-bound land. The demo version of “Frostrail” is set to be released on October 19.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/900/G090034/20261008050/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T20:56:56+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 7, 2026, FakeFish announced that it would release a demo version of its upcoming title, “Frostrail,” on October 19. Set in a barren, ice-bound wasteland, the game is an open-world survival first-person shooter in which players embark on a journey aboard an armored steam locomotive.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/010/G101096/20261008049/">
<ns1:title>The official live stream for “Jigoku Kōrin” will air on October 14 at 9:00 p.m. Reiya Takahashi and Shōtarō Morikubo will appear.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/010/G101096/20261008049/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T20:43:01+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　The Beppu City Public Works Bureau will stream the official live broadcast of the IP project “Jigoku Kōrin” starting at 9:00 p.m. on October 14. The program will feature Reiya Takahashi, who plays Umi, and Shōtarō Morikubo, who plays Ryūmaki, and will include a cast discussion and special segments.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104886/20261008046/">
<ns1:title>While enjoying shopping on a fictional online store, strange items begin to appear on the shelves... The text-based psychological horror adventure game "Cursed Shopping" is now available as a demo.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104886/20261008046/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T20:34:32+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　TOBONGAME today began distributing a demo version of "Cursed Shopping," a psychological horror adventure game for PC currently in development, on Steam. In this game, as you shop on a fictional online store, strange items begin to appear; by investigating them, you gradually uncover the full story behind a certain incident.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/004/G100451/20261008045/">
<ns1:title>Details Announced for Nijisanji's Girls Idol Event, "Girls Idol Festival ~Connecting Rainbows, Finding the Future~"</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/004/G100451/20261008045/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T20:27:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　On October 7, 2026, ANYCOLOR announced details for the live event “Nijisanji Girls Idol Festival: Connecting Rainbows, Finding the Future,” scheduled to take place over two days—December 19 and 20—at Hall 5 of Intex Osaka in Osaka City.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/456/G045622/20261008044/">
