<dc:date>2026-10-08T20:17:58+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>

</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/609/G060942/20261008042/">
<ns1:title>"ARC Raiders" Launches Major Update "Frozen Trail." The new snow-covered map "Pendora Pass" and three new enemy types make their debut.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/609/G060942/20261008042/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T20:09:14+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Nexon today rolled out the major update "FrozenTrail" for the PvPvE extraction shooter "ARCRaiders." The update adds the new map "Pendora Pass" and three new enemy types. The game will be free to play through October 12, and a beta test for PvE matchmaking will begin on the 13th.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999106/20261008004/">
<ns1:title>In the latest video from Washagana TV, we introduce the "Super Asurada 01" figure, released to commemorate the 35th anniversary of the anime, which features transformation functions and sound effects.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/991/G999106/20261008004/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T20:00:00+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　Today, the latest episode of the web show “Washagana TV,” featuring voice actor Yuichi Nakamura and freelance writer Mafia Kajita, was released. In this episode, as part of Nakamura’s “Personal Collection” segment, he introduces a figure of the “Super Asurada 01” from the anime “New Century GPX Cyber Formula.”
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/903/G090320/20261008040/">
<ns1:title>"Neon Abyss 2," a cyber-mythology roguelike for up to four players, has officially launched. It features a final boss and new modes.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/903/G090320/20261008040/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T19:39:17+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　VeewoGames officially released the cyber-mythological roguelike action game "NeonAbyss 2" today (October 8, 2026). The official release includes the final boss, "Theia: God of Vanity," and a new mode called "Storm Breach."
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/999/G999903/20261008041/">
<ns1:title>"JuJu Densetsu" (International Title: "Toki") is making a comeback. This is not a remake, but rather a plan to port the game to game consoles and PCs that were not supported at the time.</ns1:title>
<ns1:link>https://www.4gamer.net/games/999/G999903/20261008041/</ns1:link>
<dc:date>2026-10-08T19:34:07+09:00</dc:date>
<ns1:description>
　NEWOLDPIXELS announced that it has signed a licensing agreement with Microids regarding "The Legend of JuJu" (international title: "Toki"). The plan is not to create a remake, but to make the original version playable on game consoles and computers that did not support it at the time.
</ns1:description>
</ns1:item>

	<ns1:item rdf:about="https://www.4gamer.net/games/048/G104884/20261008039/">
<ns1:title>In a city inspired by 1990s China, players complete tasks while driving utility vehicles such as small trucks and taxis. The driving game "SHIFU: Traffic Masters" is now available as a demo.</ns1:title>
